      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We can rewrite the equation as $5(x+2) = x^3-2x^2-8x$.\nExpanding and simplifying, we get $x^3-3x^2-16x=0$.\nFactoring out an $x$, we get $x(x^2-3x-16)=0$.\nThis gives us three possible solutions for $x$: $x=0$, $x=3\\pm\\sqrt{33}$.\nThe sum of these solutions is $0+9-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{33}}=\\boxed{9}$.\nThe answer is: 9",
